line	<str>Use the blood potion on the door , open and search the chest to receive the old notes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Safalaan with the notes .</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the Myreque hideout and speak to Safalaan to start a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Defeat the abomination. (Note: Complete the post-fight dialogue until the point where the Myreque leave or you'll have to return to the Hideout.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Burgh de Rott, and take the boat to Meiyerditch.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to Old Man Ral's house in the centre of southern Meiyerditch. Enter the secondary Myreque base via the trapdoor in the north room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Vertida Sefalatis.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read Flaygian's notes.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you haven't made another rod of Ivandis, you can now return to Veliaf Hurtz at Burgh de Rott hideout to reclaim it.</str>
line	
line	<str>In Old Man Ral's basement, search the nearby crates to find a silver sickle (b) and a chain.</str>
line	
line	<str>Attach the emerald to the sickle to create an emerald sickle (b).</str>
line	
line	<str>Then, cast Lvl-2 Enchant on the emerald sickle, or use an enchant emerald or jade tablet on it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Finally, use the chain on the Enchanted emerald sickle (b) or the rod of Ivandis to create the Ivandis flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Go to the <col=800000>Theatre of Blood</col> (run east of <col=800000>Old Man Ral</col>'s house and go through the Ver Sinhaza castle walls) and speak to <col=800000>Kael Forshaw</col> by the noticeboard.</col>
